sensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "dbbc5de3ef8c29768a232aea7b43975fa7bc59ba40d129bf0abc72d1b1114f91", "hash": "53345a10327526f3367c48935d00405befdfb44f5ffef8a7d69dfae85febce01"}, {"seq": 3152, "time": "2026-10-29T05:32:08.395026+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-219ee794824c4408\",\"previous_head\":\"c1abd6326d6c930d07a114388f6485c8f679173051ce3a8b74f56aebd7d92f4b\",\"process_id\":2451,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-219ee794824c4408", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "c1abd6326d6c930d07a114388f6485c8f679173051ce3a8b74f56aebd7d92f4b", "hash": "dbbc5de3ef8c29768a232aea7b43975fa7bc59ba40d129bf0abc72d1b1114f91"}, {"seq": 3151,